The original loop called `fields.size()` and `fields[i]` on every iteration. This version reads the vector's begin and end pointers once and walks them directly, so each step is just a pointer increment and a compare. Fields are still checked in the same order, so it returns the same `Field*` (or `FIT_NULL`) as before.

```cpp
Field* Mesg::GetField(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    Field* it = fields.data();
    Field* const end = it + fields.size();

    for (; it != end; ++it)
    {
        if (it->GetNum() == fieldNum)
            return it;
    }

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```